 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? A balanced meal is the easy part. Split meals into three parts, one for each of the macronutrients, protein, carbs and fats. That's fine, she can have yellow food for one meal and mix it up for the others. The point is she eats something every few hours. Coffee and bread are both fine, but she might be hungry an hour later. A yogurt with fruit or porridge with milk keeps her eating. Letting her stir the pot and put the lid on builds her confidence. It's easier than it looks.",
